<Project>
  <!--
    MSVC PDB write serialisation.

    Two CL.EXE processes writing one .PDB makes the second fail with
    "C1041: cannot open program database" or "C1090: PDB API call failed",
    even under MSBuild -m:1, because MSBuild compiles a project's sources in
    more than one batch. /FS routes every write through mspdbsrv so they queue
    instead of colliding.

    ClCompile ONLY. /FS on <Link> is not valid for the static-library
    (lib.exe) targets this repo also builds. The PDB write race is entirely a
    cl.exe-side concern, so that is the only place /FS belongs.

    This lives here rather than in each vcxproj because the vendored projects
    (imgui, yaml-cpp, GLFW, ...) are regenerated from upstream and would lose
    a per-project edit; Directory.Build.props is imported by all of them.

    Do NOT also set MinimalRebuild=false here. It swaps MSBuild into
    TrackedVCToolTask.DeleteFiles, which then fails with MSB6003 on the tlog
    cleanup, trading one intermittent failure for another.
  -->
  <ItemDefinitionGroup>
    <ClCompile>
      <!--
        /bigobj raises the section count the object format allows.

        Without it the editor build dies with "MSB6006: CL.exe exited with
        code 1" and NO diagnostic, right after "Generating Code...". That is
        during LTCG codegen, where an object-file section overflow surfaces as
        a bare process exit rather than a compile error. The engine passed the
        default budget as pybind11, NVRHI and the Visual Blocks machinery came
        in.

        Global, not per-project, because the symptom is invisible: no error
        line, just a compiler that vanishes. The module project already passed
        /bigobj locally and built fine while the editor did not, which made
        this look like a flaky build rather than a missing flag.

        NB: no double hyphens in this comment. XML forbids them inside a
        comment, and an illegal comment is a MSB4024 that stops EVERY project
        in the repo from loading.
      -->
      <AdditionalOptions>/FS /bigobj %(AdditionalOptions)</AdditionalOptions>
    </ClCompile>
  </ItemDefinitionGroup>
</Project>
